  "solution": {
    "text": "Centre &amp; radius of <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>89</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> are <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> &amp; <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> respectively<br /><br />Centre &amp; radius of <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>42</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> are <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3,7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> &amp; <math><mn>4</mn></math> respectively<br /><br />Distance between the centres of circles is <math><msqrt><msup><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>≤</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>≤</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mn>21</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />Hence, the number of possible values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to <math><mn>18</mn></math>&nbsp;"
